Easy Snacks for Period Cravings

Cravings can feel especially noticeable during your period. You may want something sweet, salty, crunchy, or comforting. Instead of trying to completely eliminate cravings, you can enjoy your favourite foods while also keeping nutritious snacks available.

Banana with peanut butter is an easy combination. Bananas provide carbohydrates and potassium, while peanut butter adds protein and healthy fats. It takes only a few minutes to prepare and can be useful when you need an afternoon snack.

Yoghurt with fruit is another simple choice. Add chopped banana, apple, papaya, or berries to yoghurt and sprinkle some nuts or seeds on top. This gives you a mixture of protein, carbohydrates, and fats.

Roasted chickpeas can be a good option when you want something crunchy. You can season them with spices according to your taste. Chickpeas provide plant-based protein and fibre and can be prepared in advance.

Nuts and seeds are convenient for busy days. Almonds, walnuts, peanuts, pumpkin seeds, and sunflower seeds can be kept in a small container and eaten when hunger strikes. Because nuts and seeds are energy-dense, a modest portion can make a satisfying snack.

If you are craving something sweet, fruit can be an easy choice. A bowl of watermelon, grapes, orange segments, or papaya can feel refreshing. You can also enjoy a small amount of dark chocolate alongside fruit or nuts.

For savoury cravings, homemade popcorn, boiled corn, vegetable sandwiches, or sprouts chaat can be enjoyable. Adding herbs, spices, lemon, or chutney can make simple snacks more interesting.

There is no rule that says you cannot eat your favourite comfort foods during your period. Pizza, noodles, ice cream, or sweets can still fit into an overall balanced diet. The goal is not perfection but variety.

Hydration is also worth remembering. Keep water nearby and drink regularly. Sometimes thirst can be mistaken for hunger, especially when you are busy.

Along with food, make your period-care supplies easy to access. Keeping a few sanitary pads in your bag can be helpful when you are at college, work, shopping, or travelling. A small period-care pouch can keep everything organised.

The right sanitary pad is a personal choice. Consider comfort, absorbency, fit, and how well the product works with your normal flow.

